 },
 "method": "Landsat Collection 2 Level-2 surface reflectance (USGS, via Microsoft Planetary Computer), Landsat 5 TM / 7 ETM+ / 8-9 OLI, 30 m pixels resampled to a 15 m grid. Per year: up to 4 dry-season (Jun-Oct) days whose box is >=85 % clear after the QA_PIXEL cloud / dilated-cloud / shadow mask (Landsat 7 after May 2003 only as a last resort, >=60 %); if fewer than 2 such days, the window widens to the neighbouring years. Water = per-pixel median MNDWI (green - SWIR 1.6 um)/(green + SWIR) > 0 over the clear days; land = the rest. land_lost_ha = land in the base year minus land in that year inside the fixed site box. permanent_land = never water on any clear day. Shoreline: each row of the walk box from the west (sea) edge to the first run of 3 land pixels (45 m) on the median composite; shore_advance_m_normal is the mean row shift converted to a distance square to the base-year shoreline. CAVEATS: MNDWI cannot tell sea from flooded fish ponds (tambak): ponds full of water count as water, dry or vegetated pond beds and bunds count as land, so 'land' here is dry ground, villages, roads, mangroves, rice and dry pond beds, and part of the land loss before ~2000 is ponds being flooded, not open sea. Tide state on each day moves the wet line on the mudflats; single years are noisy, read decades. Mangrove belts planted after ~2005 count as land. Distances are ground metres."
}